    explanation:
      'FENa = [(48 × 4.5) / (138 × 85)] × 100 = 2.7%. FENa >2% indicates intrinsic AKI (acute tubular necrosis in this case).',
    calculationHint: 'FENa = [(UNa × SCr) / (SNa × UCr)] × 100',
