        sodium: 132,
        potassium: 5.4,
        chloride: 95,
        bicarbonate: 8,
        bun: 32,
        creatinine: 1.4,
        glucose: 580,
      },
    },
    correctAnswer: 29,
    unit: 'mEq/L',
    marginOfError: 2,
    explanation:
      'Anion Gap = 132 - (95 + 8) = 29 mEq/L. Severely elevated anion gap with low bicarbonate = DKA (ketoacids causing high anion gap metabolic acidosis).',
